[{:db/id "q-71035/selection/128f133c09c9169ec696351407f6ba55274fcffc6dca0a8cf556a810cbc2740e" :answer/id #uuid "0b386dad-4a3c-56e4-818f-7510956f92d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+6}{10}=\\frac{z-2}{3},\\,x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "56e4a3e0-599b-529a-8e1f-d05e2098f1bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035/selection/a04487df868b128cceeb91685baa03a87cf3d41a6c3821ffe67d096a3072a52c" :answer/id #uuid "406d740c-121e-538b-afa2-2765c1db1434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-6}{10}=\\frac{z+2}{3},\\,x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035/selection/b181d9f3d13b811fc22095214dec3f17ca6e8fbf484e22860bd20d4c1bec6f88" :answer/id #uuid "bccab0f6-7b5b-5364-952d-6bf1f9aca950" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-3}=\\frac{y+10}{6}=\\frac{z+3}{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035/selection/09e1c49c7db89a5f8686de345abbf64b76acb29ee5260ad4ba36c083b887f929" :answer/id #uuid "c9d1adf0-7fc8-5474-a3d4-45d2421830f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-3}=\\frac{y-10}{6}=\\frac{z-3}{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a074eef-ca0d-5612-93e1-0bf70c937bb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71035/selection/a04487df868b128cceeb91685baa03a87cf3d41a6c3821ffe67d096a3072a52c" :answer-field/choices ["q-71035/selection/128f133c09c9169ec696351407f6ba55274fcffc6dca0a8cf556a810cbc2740e" "q-71035/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" "q-71035/selection/a04487df868b128cceeb91685baa03a87cf3d41a6c3821ffe67d096a3072a52c" "q-71035/selection/b181d9f3d13b811fc22095214dec3f17ca6e8fbf484e22860bd20d4c1bec6f88" "q-71035/selection/09e1c49c7db89a5f8686de345abbf64b76acb29ee5260ad4ba36c083b887f929"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71035" :question/id #uuid "e46ec1f2-b47a-5934-a8b0-4cd40878864d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71035" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{0}=\\frac{y-6}{10}=\\frac{z-(-2)}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{0}=\\frac{y-6}{10}=\\frac{z+2}{3},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-3:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6+10t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-3$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-6}{10}=\\frac{z+2}{3},\\,x=-3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71035/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71035"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection/485cc86006a3788a3140c2754b26d5768c021613f4954b48dccb7ecbabff9da0" :answer/id #uuid "3897fd54-276a-5ac3-bc8b-8fd562da2978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z-7}{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection/e6684908745cc6be1503c516df0574e98ad9e18119998d583d57c813532ed8b0" :answer/id #uuid "dd2c85dd-97d4-5591-a4ff-64505c1f57a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z+7}{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection/4e250ae858437876dc7703db081f4538128b9d3f951d80ebcabd98482f07e2de" :answer/id #uuid "3142d4df-83f3-5b3e-b02e-b019a6a51a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{1}=\\frac{y+1}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection/b2684ff48e564a1619f55169256ed5daa34e71833f558667de4ef5ddf84bb93f" :answer/id #uuid "6d1be165-4655-58ac-9314-66221f485807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{1}=\\frac{y+1}{5}=\\frac{z-1}{-7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection/3832c829edfa4147abcd0a30705f8dbd8855f00f34d083c872d55d82b26c2902" :answer/id #uuid "683a1f91-97ca-5d0a-8123-29001dc443fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{-1}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z+7}{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd54e826-0b6b-5cc5-ace9-aa00b7b0e240" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127401/selection/e6684908745cc6be1503c516df0574e98ad9e18119998d583d57c813532ed8b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-127401/selection/485cc86006a3788a3140c2754b26d5768c021613f4954b48dccb7ecbabff9da0" "q-127401/selection/e6684908745cc6be1503c516df0574e98ad9e18119998d583d57c813532ed8b0" "q-127401/selection/4e250ae858437876dc7703db081f4538128b9d3f951d80ebcabd98482f07e2de" "q-127401/selection/b2684ff48e564a1619f55169256ed5daa34e71833f558667de4ef5ddf84bb93f" "q-127401/selection/3832c829edfa4147abcd0a30705f8dbd8855f00f34d083c872d55d82b26c2902"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127401" :question/id #uuid "a969f145-2e3a-5f84-b3c0-cc06d4a6d169" :question/math-academy-id "q-127401" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t \\\\ y=5-t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-2t \\\\ 5-t \\\\ -7+t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(1,5,-7)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-1,1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z-(-7)}{1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z+7}{1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127401/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44cf726-a4a6-5ac9-a63c-7464fe5566c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection/6c1927d1d3f7075c8c4a99e8f220c46099f71109a22ac02845327ae7171dfd23" :answer/id #uuid "6100088c-66a2-5deb-894a-7e581f4dbf65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection/3b8aa360c38dc500535cf5e059e588ecac5615d6bb4c3f01dad4c5a046b2ff55" :answer/id #uuid "46c4a7d1-90a6-5d23-9fa2-e93bd90263f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection/84c88accc380cb5ec459d758128e05ab6676e8efd46fc9bc8f632cbf926834f9" :answer/id #uuid "39260a09-41e3-5270-bd4d-f5b8d759a827" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{1}=\\frac{z+1}{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection/ca35169af51aac3a040f07b39b6dcb75eca40e1e4cc53e73cf241101dcb7028e" :answer/id #uuid "5c413646-05d6-55ad-87c5-747e4f1de4d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-1}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection/c9744f15811bdfdb168f8968640eea69ff2909ac8be7b41df1891459d717009b" :answer/id #uuid "3c58ff24-0cef-5c21-b9d9-70883af5c10c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "055c498e-43ab-5b42-9766-32df873a037b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127410/selection/c9744f15811bdfdb168f8968640eea69ff2909ac8be7b41df1891459d717009b" :answer-field/choices ["q-127410/selection/6c1927d1d3f7075c8c4a99e8f220c46099f71109a22ac02845327ae7171dfd23" "q-127410/selection/3b8aa360c38dc500535cf5e059e588ecac5615d6bb4c3f01dad4c5a046b2ff55" "q-127410/selection/84c88accc380cb5ec459d758128e05ab6676e8efd46fc9bc8f632cbf926834f9" "q-127410/selection/ca35169af51aac3a040f07b39b6dcb75eca40e1e4cc53e73cf241101dcb7028e" "q-127410/selection/c9744f15811bdfdb168f8968640eea69ff2909ac8be7b41df1891459d717009b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127410" :question/id #uuid "57e97057-e8bc-5a18-a1e1-2b43855aa175" :question/math-academy-id "q-127410" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=-5t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,-1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y-0}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127410/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44cf726-a4a6-5ac9-a63c-7464fe5566c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection/a0a19bb782663fa5ea9ea097d51c3860edd3ef74363c7f1d6104a3d356fce716" :answer/id #uuid "212c1a75-9740-5370-b2ac-d752a8080b74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection/c810e86b804543f9ad6b3aa293306614121b96615bcad752297e62c25052049d" :answer/id #uuid "806ffd2b-5edb-58f0-801b-10e7ccac1f4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{5}=\\frac{z+5}{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection/5bcfc6acf922e8e01034704301ebf774fcae34502af834601c6b2c33c4fb7c3a" :answer/id #uuid "bc74b0cd-f228-5745-8402-f886f256fcfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y+4}{-5}=\\frac{z+5}{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection/27078be6770280ad1366391a9a11eab200f9264c1c1c413b78c6b296bc8f0d0b" :answer/id #uuid "12f09e9e-3f23-5403-911e-738d2b9c46bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{-8}=\\frac{y-4}{-3}=\\frac{z-5}{-5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection/65a50f6fdd320ca88e5d50a3706c907f2491f73bf1565a03faeeac7ac5fa1b02" :answer/id #uuid "29c345eb-080c-5d4d-8336-39f30eeb7f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{-8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8616c8-9d1c-5552-be85-685b70032d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127466/selection/a0a19bb782663fa5ea9ea097d51c3860edd3ef74363c7f1d6104a3d356fce716" :answer-field/choices ["q-127466/selection/a0a19bb782663fa5ea9ea097d51c3860edd3ef74363c7f1d6104a3d356fce716" "q-127466/selection/c810e86b804543f9ad6b3aa293306614121b96615bcad752297e62c25052049d" "q-127466/selection/5bcfc6acf922e8e01034704301ebf774fcae34502af834601c6b2c33c4fb7c3a" "q-127466/selection/27078be6770280ad1366391a9a11eab200f9264c1c1c413b78c6b296bc8f0d0b" "q-127466/selection/65a50f6fdd320ca88e5d50a3706c907f2491f73bf1565a03faeeac7ac5fa1b02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127466" :question/id #uuid "68f94319-5269-5c99-8ae2-6775bc4441c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-127466" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/assets/1647eb5cca32c6fdc99e23507db151a8299b29bfa70ebfbaa941e17fe4638586.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,4,5)$ and $Q(7,-1,2).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-1,2⟩-⟨-1,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127466/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc74baa-313b-51e7-8ae1-5e9fe0761256"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127466"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection/159645b1aa054632f28f55961bc3b38a82dc85d06f0d8f9b37fe05e330778d10" :answer/id #uuid "9640fe34-6da0-52cf-9be1-a13d9cbccd0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{-2}=\\frac{y+1}{4},\\,z=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection/196d8b6e550cd5b53391d1e321f06fb1f6da398c9eca83124287111cc606a36e" :answer/id #uuid "155e553b-f3f1-523a-ba0f-6a59dc2489d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-1}{-4},\\,z=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection/561b2733aab05e0307b7094b0e7c3f0f36fad5c4f2847dc42e79ee706c2525e4" :answer/id #uuid "28d38cad-94b5-5266-8b60-2ced65e75903" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2},\\,z=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection/2eb3ca854b3f33dfd1167b3890984044947e42777fefb208e7dae30e44c1413b" :answer/id #uuid "3a979667-d100-5f70-aaec-f521fe120305" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{-2}=\\frac{y+1}{-4},\\,z=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection/b1d2ddeecc5017c7e1e311e970faad1cc4a9da347f57eb7fb2194fbad8e94f5f" :answer/id #uuid "5466bdda-44a7-522d-ac23-7fefa26806d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{4},\\,z=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61f89ed3-9f36-5ed7-a075-840c44199506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127527/selection/561b2733aab05e0307b7094b0e7c3f0f36fad5c4f2847dc42e79ee706c2525e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-127527/selection/159645b1aa054632f28f55961bc3b38a82dc85d06f0d8f9b37fe05e330778d10" "q-127527/selection/196d8b6e550cd5b53391d1e321f06fb1f6da398c9eca83124287111cc606a36e" "q-127527/selection/561b2733aab05e0307b7094b0e7c3f0f36fad5c4f2847dc42e79ee706c2525e4" "q-127527/selection/2eb3ca854b3f33dfd1167b3890984044947e42777fefb208e7dae30e44c1413b" "q-127527/selection/b1d2ddeecc5017c7e1e311e970faad1cc4a9da347f57eb7fb2194fbad8e94f5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127527" :question/id #uuid "660620a9-8a2e-5788-8e01-c31fb36aca66" :question/math-academy-id "q-127527" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/assets/8722b93655e069e2f35147b572c16ed7af408a86f8a88597c79aea8fe59e9c4d.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(2,-1,3)$ and $Q(4,-3,3).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-3,3⟩-⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{0}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{z-3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=3.$ For example, our two points $P(2,-1,3)$ and $Q(4,-3,3)$ both have $z$-coordinates of $z=3.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-3}{0}$ part and instead write $z=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2},\\,z=3.\n$$" 